-Original text symbols ☰ / • / ✓ supplement localized labels; no third-party icon
-library is redistributed. This is a minimal native icon vocabulary, not completion
-of the supplied 122-icon library. Dedicated graph/editor interaction widgets and
+Native 16-unit line icons in `desktop/icons.rs` supplement localized command
+labels (folder, add, panels, search, settings, file and activity). Evidence symbols
+remain redundant with state text. No third-party icon library is redistributed;
+this bounded vocabulary does not complete the supplied 122-icon library. Dedicated graph/editor interaction widgets and
 full tree/table icon coverage remain future visual work; backend absence alone does
 not prove their design complete. Font provenance and bundled OFL are recorded in
 font-provenance.json. Screen-reader semantics have not been verified.
@@ -35,3 +36,50 @@ inspector flank the primary canvas; otherwise the composition stacks.
 `relationship_map` uses declared Cargo dependencies, with a stacked alternative below
 1200. `agent_roles` provides a role/responsibility/instance table with no invented
 agent activity. Existing theme roles and body sizes apply; no new asset dependency.
+
+## Enterprise chrome successor — 2026-11-16
+
+At 1100+ logical width a single context row combines navigation, identity,
+project context and presentation commands. Below that width commands use a
+second row to preserve their labels. Busy cancellation retains its own visible
+control region. The status footer is a single compact row. S01/S02 context
+separators have bounded height; unrestricted vertical rules must not expand
+header rows. The recent/action sidebar is 368 units wide at900+ and otherwise
+uses available width; its scroll owns focus reveal.
+
+Preferences default to theme/density and a concise session-scope explanation.
+The existing Details toggle reveals noninteractive typography/color/state examples;
+control IDs and effect contracts stay the same. Task evidence badges and backend
+implementation notices are absent from S13/S14.
+
+## Desktop navigation interaction — 2026-11-17
+
+`desktop/splitter.rs` owns only hit testing/cursor/start on a6-unit handle; Desktop
+owns transient drag/width lifecycle and observes move/release independent of event
+capture status. Pointer grab offset prevents jumps. End/cancel paths include
+CursorLeft/Unfocused/Escape/navigation/command/resize. Min200/max420 and
+windowwidth−326 preserve the primary region; rail52 keeps actual destination
+controls. Width is remembered only for the session.
+
+`desktop/hint.rs` provides a keyboard-focus label overlay; native tooltip covers
+pointer hover. Settings272 deliberately uses hover-only text with a visible focus
+border, per the user request. Buttons215/216 reduce/increase width24 and stay in explicit
+traversal only when expanded. Ctrl+B toggles; Ctrl+Alt+arrows is optional because
+window managers can intercept it. Each destination uses its own icon geometry;
+labels and IDs remain the authority. AT conformance is not inferred from a tooltip.
+
+Project-entry correction (2026-11-17): Settings and agent-settings entries share
+one native cog renderer. S01 primary action is New project, followed by Open
+folders and disabled Clone repository with an unavailable tooltip. Recents and
+resume controls occupy the main area; narrow layouts stack actions above projects.
+Keyboard traversal follows rendered actionable order and excludes disabled Clone.
+
+## Reference translation contract — 2026-11-17
+
+Future changes use the VISUAL STUDIO 2026 ENTERPRISE baseline in DESIGN revision 5.0.
+Map source shell/tool windows to Ox navigation, document tabs, inspector and tool
+regions; map command hierarchy to existing controls and status to source-bound
+feedback. Preserve distinct hover/focus/selection/disabled/busy states, accessible
+names, keyboard routes, overflow recovery and opaque material fallbacks. Document
+any new component/variant and its actual native verification. The implemented table
+above is an inventory, not proof of fidelity to the new target.
diff --git a/docs/design/reference-coverage.md b/docs/design/reference-coverage.md
index 895fa74..84082c7 100644
--- a/docs/design/reference-coverage.md
+++ b/docs/design/reference-coverage.md
@@ -173,3 +173,46 @@ remote-development entries, branded assets and onboarding promotion are not adop
 R4/R12 remain inspiration for hierarchy; DESIGN owns roles, fonts and themes.
 Recent rows now require actual successful-open metadata under the newly authorized
 welcome contract; fictional projects remain excluded. No pixel-identical copy claimed.
+
+## Definitive identity integration — 2026-11-16
+
+The supplied `.local/assets/definitivo/README.md` and `prancha.png` were inspected.
+Identity revision identidade-definitiva-01 selects Catalisador v2 study 06,
+Valência v1 study 01 and the cotton mascot v5 study 17, with approved Ferris tag
+revision algodao-etiqueta-vetorial-05. S01 embeds byte-identical `logo-escuro.png`,
+`logo-branco.png` and `mascote-ox.png`; proportions, negative space and alpha remain
+intact. No source board, historical study, generator or `.local` path is loaded
+at runtime. Signature layout is preserved inside the artwork; its integration
+adapts to the native project-entry geometry rather than reproducing the board's
+informational captions. The mascot is raster; no vectorization/animation is claimed.
+Source/copy hashes and observed captures: [identity report](../validation/welcome-identity-20261116/report.md).
+
+## Enterprise desktop reference successor — 2026-11-16
+
+The two newly supplied IntelliJ Home captures show the same structural direction:
+window-filling context bar, slim navigation, docked project actions/recents, expansive
+neutral workspace and discreet status/tools. The maintainer contrasts these with
+the rejected Ox floating welcome card. Adopt hierarchy, restrained density and
+docked layout across native presentation; preserve DESIGN palette and IBM Plex.
+Third-party branding, clone/remote/terminal effects and unknown interaction behavior
+are not imported. Definitive OX assets remain intact with a compact signature and
+secondary mascot. Version and runtime behavior cannot be inferred from captures.
+See [enterprise report](../validation/enterprise-visual-20261116/report.md).
+
+## Windows / Visual Studio successor — 2026-11-17
+
+The maintained [Windows design analysis](windows-apps-analysis.md) inventories
+consulted sources, topics, dispositions and remaining limits. It supplies the
+source trace for DESIGN revision 5.0 and the windows-design-baseline SDD feature.
+
+| Reference | Disposition | Boundary |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| VISUAL STUDIO 2026 ENTERPRISE | mandatory primary visual base by explicit request | IDE shell/workspace hierarchy; no edition-exclusive visual claims |
+| Windows app design / Fluent | supporting principles, foundations, controls, interaction and accessibility | translated to Rust/Iced and actual target platforms |
+| R2–R13 and previous enterprise/IntelliJ references | historical/supporting, subordinate in visual conflicts | retain domain details, identity provenance and observed evidence |
+| WinUI/XAML/API samples and Windows shell integrations | implementation-specific, deferred where no Ox capability exists | no dependency or platform adoption |
+| Microsoft fonts/icons/material samples | reference only unless separately licensed/adopted | retain Plex and Ox assets |
+
+Every affected visual task must identify its actual source/version, surface/component,
+adoption or justified adaptation, and future native evidence. Documentary coverage
+does not establish visual, interaction or accessibility parity.
